MASS CONSERVATION (annual incident vs weekly sum by week_start year):
  2022: incident=54,514  weekly=54,513.6  shortfall=0.4
  2023: incident=49,687  weekly=49,687.4  shortfall=-0.4
  2024: incident=26,718  weekly=26,777.9  shortfall=-59.9
  2025: incident=7,676  weekly=7,615.6  shortfall=60.4

INCIDENT DERIVATION: cumulative[t] - cumulative[t-1] within year.
  Year boundary resets: a synthetic zero-cumulative snapshot is
  injected at Jan 1 per district, so the first real snapshot keeps
  incident = cumulative (YTD from Jan 1) and receives interval
  Jan 1 -> snapshot date; January mass enters the weekly panel.

WEEKLY REGULARIZATION: daily rate = incident / interval_days,
  uniformly distributed across interval, then summed to ISO weeks.
  Zero-incident intervals retained: no-case ISO weeks appear as
  explicit zeros (5556 weeks), preserving seasonality.

